  "summary": "The underlying storyâ€”Indigenous delegates at EMRIP in Geneva confronting compounding climate, conflict, extractivism, and legal-marginalization threatsâ€”is real and supported by the ICT/Grist intake. But the manuscript cites zero sources (no references array, the story itself never linked), misidentifies the two Grist journalists as testifying 'leaders,' launders the Conversation piece's 'multiplicative not additive' framing onto the Indigenous News Alliance story, flattens the non-Indigenous-framed Greater Horn polycrisis into an Indigenous analogy, and pads nearly every paragraph with invented causal mechanisms and generic collapse rhetoric. The thesis and evidence base are salvageable, but the repairs are substantial.",
